{
  "_comment": "High-address soak. Terra Battle truncates a pointer to 32 bits during startup; on Android layouts that hand out addresses above 4 GB that becomes a wild pointer and the process SIGSEGVs inside il2cpp init (reproduced on a Galaxy S25 / Android 17; the emulator and S23 never see it). DT_INIT_ARRAY[0] is retargeted to a cave that reserves high address space in 1 GiB / 64 MiB / 2 MiB / 64 KiB tiers until the kernel returns sub-4 GB addresses, keeps those reservations (PROT_NONE|MAP_NORESERVE, no physical memory) and then runs the original initialiser. The addend edit is plain file data in .rela.dyn, so verify reproduces it like any other byte patch.",
